From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 13:38:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] media: apple: prores: Bind the T8132 engine by
 default

The T8132 engine was kept behind apple_prores.t8132=1 until it had run on
a machine. On a J604 it now has: with the parameter set at module load it
probed with its initialization rows, encoded 30 4K 4:2:2 frames in 85 ms
and 300 in 386 ms, ffmpeg decoded all 30 back, and the kernel logged no
error. Without the parameter its node stayed unbound.

Turn the parameter on by default. apple_prores.t8132=0 keeps the engine
off as before. A machine without the per-machine initialization file
logs one line at probe and leaves the engine off, as on T6041.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
---
 .../media/platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c | 14 +++++++-------
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+), 7 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c b/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c
index 5b15bdf361..8c66a0bbc1 100644
--- a/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c
+++ b/drivers/media/platform/apple/prores/apple-prores-drv.c
@@ -1433,15 +1433,15 @@ static struct platform_driver apr_driver = {
 	},
 };
 /*
- * The T8132 (M4) engine binds only on request: apple_prores.t8132=1 on the
- * kernel command line (or at module load). Off by default, so nothing binds
- * its node, and neither its power domain nor its windows are touched, until
- * the engine has run on the machine. A driver of its own keeps the other
- * engines as they are.
+ * The T8132 (M4) engine has its own platform driver so that it can be kept
+ * off: apple_prores.t8132=0 on the kernel command line (or at module load)
+ * leaves its node unbound, its power domain unattached and its windows
+ * unmapped. On by default; without the per-machine initialization file the
+ * probe logs one line and leaves the engine off.
  */
-static bool t8132;
+static bool t8132 = true;
 module_param(t8132, bool, 0444);
-MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132, "Bind the T8132 (M4) ProRes engine (default: off)");
+MODULE_PARM_DESC(t8132, "Bind the T8132 (M4) ProRes engine (default: on)");
 
 static const struct of_device_id apr_t8132_of_match[] = {
 	{ .compatible = "apple,t8132-prores", .data = &apr_t8132 },
-- 
